{"title":"Career Roadmap · Imaging Specialist","role":"Imaging Specialist","summary":"An Imaging Specialist in the allied-health pathway supports diagnostic imaging services by operating imaging equipment, preparing patients, acquiring high-quality images, maintaining radiation/safety protocols, performing image-quality checks, and coordinating with radiologists and other healthcare professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Radiology & Imaging Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Imaging Specialist in the allied-health pathway supports diagnostic imaging services by operating imaging equipment, preparing patients, acquiring high-quality images, maintaining radiation/safety protocols, performing image-quality checks, and coordinating with radiologists and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Indian undergraduate pathway, the relevant qualification may be B.Sc Radiology & Imaging Technology / B.Sc Medical Imaging Technology / B.Sc Radiography or an institution-specific equivalent. The exact professional title and scope vary by qualification, employer, and applicable regulations."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can span:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"X-ray"},{"text":"CT"},{"text":"MRI"},{"text":"Mammography"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Interventional imaging support"},{"text":"Ultrasound support, where qualification/scope permits"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine imaging, with additional specialized training"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"Digital imaging"},{"text":"Imaging quality and safety"}]},{"type":"note","label":"A key distinction","text":"Image acquisition and technical operation are different from radiological diagnosis. A radiographer/radiologic technologist does not automatically become a radiologist by gaining imaging experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Imaging degree, anatomy, physics, patient care, radiographic positioning and equipment fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Radiographer/Imaging Technologist → build experience across X-ray, CT and MRI"}],[{"text":"2034–2040"},{"text":"Imaging Specialist → advanced modality specialization → quality/safety expertise"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Imaging Specialist → Modality Lead → Imaging Operations/Quality Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Radiation physics"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Basic electronics"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Healthcare ethics"},{"text":"Communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electromagnetic radiation"},{"text":"X-rays"},{"text":"Image formation"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Resolution"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Image artifacts"},{"text":"Radiation exposure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Projects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic radiographic image-quality study"},{"text":"Anatomy imaging atlas"},{"text":"Radiation-safety awareness module"},{"text":"Patient preparation guide"},{"text":"Imaging workflow map"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiographic Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop competence in:"},{"type":"h","text":"X-Ray"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiographic positioning"},{"text":"Exposure factors"},{"text":"Image acquisition"},{"text":"Digital radiography"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Radiation protection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chest"},{"text":"Abdomen"},{"text":"Spine"},{"text":"Upper limb"},{"text":"Lower limb"},{"text":"Skull"},{"text":"Pelvis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"History collection relevant to imaging"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Mobility assistance"},{"text":"Contrast-related safety awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Advanced Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT physics"},{"text":"Cross-sectional anatomy"},{"text":"Protocol concepts"},{"text":"Contrast-enhanced CT"},{"text":"Image reconstruction"},{"text":"Artifacts"},{"text":"Radiation dose concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MRI"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI physics"},{"text":"Magnetic fields"},{"text":"Pulse sequences"},{"text":"T1/T2 concepts"},{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"Contraindication screening"},{"text":"Artifacts"},{"text":"Patient communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Mammography"},{"text":"Interventional imaging"},{"text":"Ultrasound workflow"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The precise scope of independent operation depends on the qualification, institution, and applicable regulations."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Clinical Imaging Integration"},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to move from equipment knowledge to safe, efficient, high-quality imaging practice."},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Referral","Patient Identification","Clinical Information Review","Safety Screening","Imaging Protocol","Patient Positioning","Image Acquisition","Image Quality Check","PACS / RIS","Radiologist Review","Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Develop Skills In"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Protocol selection within scope"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Image-quality optimization"},{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"Contrast safety workflow"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Domain Knowledge"}]},{"heading":"Radiography","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Exposure factors"},{"text":"Digital radiography"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Portable radiography"},{"text":"Radiation protection"}]}]},{"heading":"CT","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Slice thickness"},{"text":"Reconstruction"},{"text":"Windowing"},{"text":"Contrast protocols"},{"text":"Dose optimization"},{"text":"CT artifacts"}]}]},{"heading":"MRI","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI physics"},{"text":"T1/T2 weighting"},{"text":"Common pulse sequences"},{"text":"Patient screening"},{"text":"Implant safety"},{"text":"RF safety"},{"text":"Image artifacts"}]}]},{"heading":"Imaging Anatomy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Musculoskeletal anatomy"},{"text":"Neuroanatomy"},{"text":"Thoracic anatomy"},{"text":"Abdominal anatomy"},{"text":"Pelvic anatomy"},{"text":"Vascular anatomy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"This should be one of the strongest competencies."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ALARA principle"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Exposure optimization"},{"text":"Occupational monitoring"},{"text":"Patient protection"},{"text":"Equipment safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong imaging professional should always prioritize diagnostic image quality at the lowest reasonably achievable exposure, rather than simply maximizing image quality."},{"type":"h","text":"Technology Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern imaging is highly digital."},{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Digital radiography systems"},{"text":"CT workstations"},{"text":"MRI workstations"},{"text":"Microsoft Excel"},{"text":"Digital documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D visualization"},{"text":"Image post-processing"},{"text":"Imaging analytics"},{"text":"Structured workflow systems"},{"text":"AI-assisted imaging tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Optional Technical Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Medical image processing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are especially useful for future AI-imaging and medical-imaging technology roles."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Clinical imaging internship should include exposure to multiple modalities."},{"type":"h","text":"Priority Departments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"X-ray"},{"text":"CT"},{"text":"MRI"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Mammography"},{"text":"Interventional radiology support"},{"text":"Emergency imaging"},{"text":"Portable imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn More Than Machine Operation"},{"type":"p","text":"During internship, focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Safety screening"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Protocol understanding"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"Contrast workflow"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Communication with radiologists"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Projects During the Degree"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Radiographic Image Quality Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exposure parameters"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Repeat rates"},{"text":"Artifacts"},{"text":"Positioning errors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build a synthetic dashboard using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Radiation Dose Optimization"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational project comparing:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Protocol","Exposure Parameters","Image Quality","Radiation Dose","Optimization Strategy"]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to demonstrate the principle of balancing diagnostic quality and radiation exposure."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — CT Protocol Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational comparison of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Head CT"},{"text":"Chest CT"},{"text":"Abdomen CT"},{"text":"Trauma CT"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Compare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical purpose"},{"text":"Acquisition parameters"},{"text":"Contrast considerations"},{"text":"Reconstruction"},{"text":"Dose considerations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — MRI Safety System"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a digital MRI screening checklist covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Implants"},{"text":"Metallic objects"},{"text":"Devices"},{"text":"Previous procedures"},{"text":"Patient safety questions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use simulated data only."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — AI Image Classification"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational computer-vision project using a suitable public dataset."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Medical Image Dataset","Preprocessing","Image Classification Model","Performance Evaluation","Visualization","Human Review"]},{"type":"p","text":"The model should be presented as a research/educational prototype, not a clinical diagnostic system."},{"type":"h","text":"Internship & Experience Strategy"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"X-ray"},{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Patient handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT"},{"text":"MRI"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Emergency imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final Internship"},{"type":"p","text":"Aim for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multi-modality exposure"},{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"Digital imaging"},{"text":"Image-quality optimization"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Equipment workflows"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After the relevant imaging qualification and applicable internship/eligibility requirements, possible roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiographer"},{"text":"Radiology Technologist"},{"text":"Medical Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"X-Ray Technologist"},{"text":"CT Technologist"},{"text":"MRI Technologist"},{"text":"Diagnostic Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"Imaging Department Technician/Technologist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience and modality specialization:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Imaging Technologist"},{"text":"CT Specialist"},{"text":"MRI Specialist"},{"text":"Imaging Quality Specialist"},{"text":"Modality Supervisor"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Radiologist is a separate physician pathway requiring a medical degree and specialist postgraduate training; it is not an advancement route from B.Sc/BMLT-style allied-health imaging training."},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Priority Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Multi-specialty Hospital"},{"text":"X-ray + CT + patient care"}],[{"text":"Diagnostic Imaging Centre"},{"text":"High-volume imaging + QC"}],[{"text":"Radiology Department"},{"text":"Multi-modality imaging"}],[{"text":"Trauma Centre"},{"text":"Emergency imaging"}],[{"text":"Cancer Centre"},{"text":"CT/MRI + specialized imaging"}],[{"text":"Women's Imaging Centre"},{"text":"Mammography + patient care"}],[{"text":"Research Centre"},{"text":"Imaging science + data"}],[{"text":"Medical Device Company"},{"text":"Imaging technology + applications"}],[{"text":"Teleradiology Organization"},{"text":"PACS + DICOM + digital workflow"}],[{"text":"AI Medical Imaging Company"},{"text":"Imaging + data + computer vision"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should complement the formal imaging qualification."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BLS"},{"text":"First aid"},{"text":"Radiation-safety training"},{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"CT technology"},{"text":"Contrast-safety training"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS/RIS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Medical image processing"},{"text":"3D visualization"},{"text":"Digital imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"Scientific writing"},{"text":"Medical imaging research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Medical image analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the institution and eligibility:"},{"type":"h","text":"Master's Pathways"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Medical Imaging Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc Radiology & Imaging Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc Medical Imaging"},{"text":"Master's in Medical Imaging Sciences"},{"text":"Master's in Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"Health Informatics"},{"text":"Medical Physics — where eligibility requirements are met"},{"text":"Clinical Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology-Oriented Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Degree","Clinical Imaging Experience","Medical Imaging / Technology Master's","Imaging Informatics / AI / Research","Advanced Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. CT Imaging Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT protocols"},{"text":"Dose optimization"},{"text":"Contrast-enhanced studies"},{"text":"Trauma imaging"},{"text":"3D reconstruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. MRI Imaging Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MRI protocols"},{"text":"Sequence selection"},{"text":"MRI safety"},{"text":"Artifact reduction"},{"text":"Advanced imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Interventional Imaging Technologist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Procedure support"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Sterile workflow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Mammography Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Breast imaging acquisition"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Radiation protection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Imaging Quality Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Repeat-rate reduction"},{"text":"Equipment QA"},{"text":"Dose monitoring"},{"text":"Protocol optimization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Imaging Informatics Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Workflow integration"},{"text":"Imaging data"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. AI Medical Imaging Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical image datasets"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"AI validation"},{"text":"Imaging analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"AI systems may increasingly assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Image reconstruction"},{"text":"Image enhancement"},{"text":"Workflow prioritization"},{"text":"Quality checks"},{"text":"Automated measurements"},{"text":"Detection support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The imaging professional must understand the limitations of AI and maintain appropriate human oversight."},{"type":"h","text":"Photon-Counting CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging CT technology can provide:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Improved spectral information"},{"text":"Potentially better spatial resolution"},{"text":"Material characterization"},{"text":"Dose-efficiency opportunities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates opportunities for technologists who understand advanced CT workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"AI MRI Reconstruction"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can help with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Faster acquisition"},{"text":"Image reconstruction"},{"text":"Noise reduction"},{"text":"Workflow optimization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D & Quantitative Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Future imaging workflows increasingly involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D reconstruction"},{"text":"Volumetric measurements"},{"text":"Quantitative biomarkers"},{"text":"Surgical planning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging Informatics"},{"type":"p","text":"The future imaging specialist should understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Modality","DICOM","PACS","RIS","AI / Analytics","Radiologist Workflow","Clinical Record"]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Technology Graduate","Junior Radiographer / Imaging Technologist","Clinical Imaging Technologist","Specialized Technologist","Senior Imaging Specialist","Modality Lead","Imaging Quality / Technical Lead","Imaging Department Manager","Imaging Services / Operations Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging Technologist","PACS / Imaging Informatics","Medical Imaging Data Specialist","AI / Imaging Technology Specialist","Imaging Informatics / Technology Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anatomy","patient care","positioning","imaging protocols","image-quality assessment"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging"},{"type":"flow","items":["X-ray","CT","MRI","fluoroscopy","modality-specific specialization"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"flow","items":["Radiation protection","MRI safety","contrast-safety workflow","infection prevention"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["PACS","RIS","DICOM","digital image processing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"flow","items":["3D imaging","AI-assisted imaging","quantitative imaging","imaging informatics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Power BI","basic statistics","optional Python/SQL"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient communication","attention to detail","teamwork","documentation","safety culture"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Imaging physics"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"X-ray"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"CT"},{"text":"Competent"}],[{"text":"MRI"},{"text":"Competent"}],[{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Image quality"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"Competent"}],[{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"Basic–Competent"}],[{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Equipment handling"},{"text":"Competent"}],[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"Medical image analysis"},{"text":"Basic"}],[{"text":"AI/computer vision"},{"text":"Basic exposure"}],[{"text":"Clinical internship"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Imaging portfolio"},{"text":"4–6 projects"}],[{"text":"Multi-modality exposure"},{"text":"Strong"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Radiology/Medical Imaging Technology","Clinical Internship","Radiographer/Imaging Technologist","CT/MRI Experience","Imaging Specialist","Senior Specialist/Modality Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a future-ready Imaging Specialist, the strongest combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Imaging physics","anatomy","patient safety","high-quality image acquisition","CT/MRI specialization","PACS/RIS/DICOM","radiation optimization","imaging informatics","AI-assisted imaging."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"“Imaging Specialist” is a broad career label. For a student-facing database, it is useful to map this role to Medical Imaging Technologist / Radiographer / Radiologic Technologist, with CT Specialist, MRI Specialist, or Imaging Informatics Specialist as later specializations. Radiologist should remain a separate physician career pathway."}]}]}